The command plays MIDI and RMID files using the sequencer device.
If no file name is given it will play from standard input, other‐
wise  it will play the named files.  RMID files are Standard MIDI
Files embedded in a RIFF container and can usually be found  with
the extension.  They contain some additional information in other
chunks which are not parsed by yet.  The program accepts the fol‐
lowing  options: specifies the number of the MIDI device used for
output (as listed by the flag).  There is no way  at  present  to
have map playback to more than one device.  The default is device
is  given  by  environment variable specifies the name of the se‐
quencer device.  list the possible devices without  playing  any‐
thing.   show  MIDI  file  meta  events (copyright, lyrics, etc).
force all channels to play with the single specified program  (or
instrument  patch,  range  1‐128).   Program change events in the
file will be suppressed.  There is no way at present to have  se‐
lectively  map  channels or instruments.  specifies that the MIDI
file should not be played, just  parsed.   send  an  MIDI  event.
